{
  "version": "0.9.0",
  "notes": "Hybrid compute: the always-on XemAi host remains the single source of chats, memory, research, files, feedback and tool execution, while a paired stronger Windows PC can perform authenticated Qwen inference over private Tailscale Serve HTTPS. XemAi prefers the worker when reachable and automatically falls back to the host's local Ollama if the worker is unavailable or fails mid-request. The worker is localhost-only behind Tailscale, requires a generated bearer token, exposes only health/model inventory/chat inference, and does not expose shell access, arbitrary files, the XemAi database or model pulling. Includes one-click worker/host pairing scripts, worker login autostart, runtime model/compute self-knowledge, and a live Worker vs Host compute badge.",
